3. More significant / notable bumps
-----------------------------------

These are the upgrades that are most likely to have behavioural
changes or tighter defaults and are worth explicit approval.

busybox            : 1.36.1  -> 1.37.0
  - Core userland; new features and occasional behavioural tweaks.

ca-certificates    : 20230311 -> 20250419
  - New CA bundle; affects TLS trust roots.

iproute2           : 6.8.0   -> 6.17.0
  - Netlink tooling; many incremental changes.

libcurl (curl)     : 8.7.1   -> 8.18.0
  - Larger jump within 8.x; TLS/protocol defaults may have changed.

nano               : 7.2     -> 8.6
  - User-facing editor; feature bump.

openssh            : 9.7p1   -> 10.2p1
  - Newer OpenSSH with potential deprecations/tighter security.

util-linux         : 2.39.3  -> 2.41.1
  - Affects a wide range of system utilities (mount, fdisk, etc.).


4. Notes on packages provided by BR2_EXTERNAL
---------------------------------------------

The following symbols in tp2bmc_defconfig refer to packages that come
from the external layer (BR2_EXTERNAL_TP2BMC_PATH), not from upstream
Buildroot’s package tree:

  BR2_PACKAGE_LIBOPENSSL
  BR2_PACKAGE_LIBOPENSSL_BIN
  BR2_PACKAGE_OPENSSL
  BR2_PACKAGE_IFUPDOWN_NG
  BR2_PACKAGE_BMCD
  BR2_PACKAGE_BMC_INSTALLER
  BR2_PACKAGE_BMC_UI
  BR2_PACKAGE_ROCKUSB
  BR2_PACKAGE_TPI
  BR2_PACKAGE_RASPBERRYPI_TARGET_USBBOOT

Their versions are controlled by your external package makefiles, so
they are not automatically changed by updating Buildroot from 2024.05.1
to 2026.02. They will, however, be rebuilt against the newer base
(toolchain, headers, libraries), and should be smoke-tested after the
upgrade.


5. Suggested approval stance
----------------------------

- Safe / unchanged: all packages listed in section 1.
- Approved-with-normal-testing: minor upgrades in section 2.
- Require explicit sign-off:
  - busybox, openssh, libcurl, util-linux, iproute2,
    ca-certificates, nano, mtd-utils.

These approvals (or decisions to pin specific versions where Buildroot
allows it) should be reflected in the updated defconfig when migrating
to Buildroot 2026.02.


6. Step 4 – Kernel 6.8.12 verification (done)
--------------------------------------------

- Kernel version pinned to 6.8.12 in tp2bmc_defconfig:
  BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CUSTOM_VERSION=y
  BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CUSTOM_VERSION_VALUE="6.8.12"
  (Buildroot 2026.02 default is 6.18.12; pinning keeps existing
   patches and ITS unchanged.)

- Kernel headers version check fixed via defconfig (no Buildroot patch):
  BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_LINUX_HEADERS_CUSTOM_6_8=y
  so the toolchain uses 6.8.x headers and the check expects 6.8.x,
  avoiding "expected 2.6.x, got 6.8.x".

- ITS: tp2bmc/board/tp2bmc/turing-pi2.its correctly references
  "turingpi 6.8.12" and kernel image "kernel6_8" / zImage.

- Patches: BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_PATCH points to
  $(BR2_EXTERNAL_TP2BMC_PATH)/patches/linux (no version subdir).
  Patches in that directory target 6.8: 0001-regulator-fixed-*,
  0002-gpio-aggregator-*, i2c.patch, realtek-switch.patch,
  Add-support-for-Allwinner-PWM-*.

- linux_defconfig and DTS paths unchanged; no edits required.

A full patch audit (buildroot_patches + tp2bmc/patches/linux) is in
docs/patch-audit.md.

